    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i just updated my A records for a client site but the new IP isnt showing up for me yet. why does it take so long for dns changes to actually work everywhere?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "DNS changes can take time (known as propagation) because your computer's local \"cache\" still holds the old IP address. Additionally, web servers and third-party sites often cache DNS records themselves, so even after your browser clears its cache, others may still see the old data for hours or days. Finally, your current ISP itself might cache DNS responses separately, which is why your network might appear to resolve the old IP just now.",
      "source": "target",
