    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "makes sense. so it's basically just a delay while all these different servers update their lists? is there any way to force it to update faster or do i just have to wait it out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, it is essentially a delay as many global servers and intermediate caches begin refreshing their records based on your specific TTL (Time to Live) settings. While you cannot directly force external sites to update instantly, you can speed up the process by using the `nslookup` or `dig` commands on your own computer to force a refresh of your ISP's cache immediately. Additionally, setting a lower TTL beforehand for your next change would have reduced the propagation time for future updates. For current changes, simply waiting a few hours is usually the only reliable method.",
      "source": "target",
